{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "A Comedy of Errors"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Friendly Advice"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le10ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Future Perfect Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future Perfect Continuous tense to talk about an action in the future that is unfinished the time another action in the future starts. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"underline\">Future Perfect Continuous</span>, you can sometimes think of it as the Present Perfect Continuous, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future. </br> With the Future Perfect Continuous, an action in the future is unfinished by the time another action in the future starts. It is most often used with an expression of time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: </br>subject+will have been + present participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br></br> <span class=\"strong\">I will have been using</span> this online dating website for 6 months by this time next week. </br>Vanessa <span class=\"strong\">will have been working</span> at Bistro 88 for two years next month."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I <span class=\"strong\">will have been dating </span>him for a year by this time next week."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I<span class=\"strong\"> will have been waiting</span> for her for three hours by six o'clock."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before the date, I imagine that we <span class=\"strong\">will have been sailing</span> on the open ocean, or we <span class=\"strong\">will have been driving</span> in the country or that we <span class=\"strong\">will have been sunning ourselves</span> on some exotic beach prior to meeting the guy."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Degrees of Necessity"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">must</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have (got)</span> to to express necessities in the past or in the present. </br>You use the negative forms of these modals (<span class=\"italic\">needn't, don't have to</span>)   to express absence of necessity in the past or in the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Must</span> refers to a necessary condition that comes from the subject and may be directed at the subject or the person the subject is talking to or about. It is used to express a strong necessity. <ul>Example:  </br><span class=\"italic\">You must cut sugar out of your diet.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have (got)  to</span> expresses external obligations, which come from outside of the subject. These may be rules and regulations over which the subject has no control. It is used to express necessity in a lower degree than with must. <ul>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">You have to tell her your true feelings.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of obligation is expressed with the <span class=\"strong\">negative form of have to</span>, not with mustn't. <ul>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">You don't have to drink so much coffee every day.</span></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by negative form of <span class=\"italic\">need</span>. It is generally used as a main verb in the construction <span class=\"italic\">don't need to</span>, but sometimes can be used as a modal, like <span class=\"italic\">needn't</span>. The infinitive after the modal verb \"needn't\" is used without the particle \"to\".  </br>Compare these sentences: </br><span class=\"italic\">You don't need to rush into a relationship right now. </br>You needn't rush into a relationship right now.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is a list of modals of necessity:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"necessity lack of necessity (negative)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You have to tell her. You don't have to make a reservation.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"strong necessity prohibition (negative)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We must meet after eight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ought to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"strong advisability\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You ought ought to tell her that you're not into her.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"strong advisability\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You should have set this girl straight a long time ago.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have to tell her your true feelings Peter."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You mustn't hide how you feel inside. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to tell her how much you like her right here."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You mustn't drink diet soda."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Peter remember you must not eat sugar. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to dip ones big toe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to try something a little bit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have dipped my big toe into politics. Just to try it out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you call a radio show!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "candidate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who wants a new position"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He is a good candidate for promotion don't you think?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tad"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a little"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am a tad under 200 lbs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prescription"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a written direction by a  doctor to a  pharmacist for the preparation of medicine for a patient "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Doctor, could  you please renew my prescription, please?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ingest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to eat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I ingested a lot of vitamins."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "online handle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "internet name"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My online handle is SNOOP564."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le10ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss common problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read about  common online dating problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give advice to people's problems using words showing degrees of necessity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I role play this activity with a partner and classmates."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "In pairs, discuss some common online dating problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a radio show where you are the hosts. You  give people advice on their online dating problems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Research common online dating problems people have."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use degrees of necessity to help with your advice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 12 - 15 lines."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Role-play with your classmates."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn10le10ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn10le10ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Host Annetta</span>: As the listeners know, I have dipped my big toe into the online dating world and after this weekend, I will have gone on 10 first dates.\n</br></br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Dr. Dana</span>: Have you found any possible true romance candidates?\n</br></br><span class=\"strong\">\nHost Annetta</span>: Not yet. They have all been nice guys.  I really need to stop setting my expectations so high. Before the date, I imagine that we will have been sailing on the open ocean, or we will have been driving in the country or that we will have been sunning ourselves on some exotic beach prior to meeting the guy. But reality can never live up to my imagination.\n</br></br>\nI think I've just got to lower my expectations a tad.  Let's just hope in a couple of months, I will have had a couple of high caliber dates and hopefully by this time next year, I will have at least found a boyfriend! Our first caller tonight is Peter from Boston.", "id": 1}, {"time": "51250", "image": "engenn10le10ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hi ...I'm calling about a problem I have. I wanted to send a text to put off a girl I don't like. Unfortunately, I sent  it to a girl I have a real connection with.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Host Annetta</span>: Oh man.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Dr. Dana</span>: Have you been drinking Peter?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: No, I just want to let this girl know that I am very sorry and I think I really like her. What should I do?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Host Annetta</span>: You have to tell her your true feelings Peter. You mustn't hide how you feel inside. Otherwise you will go through life always in a cloud of self-doubt, always wondering if you made the right choice.  Right Dr. Dana?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Dr. Dana</span>: Peter are you taking any prescription medication?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: What? \u2026 No. So how do I do that?", "id": 2}, {"time": "94600", "image": "engenn10le10ob07re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Host Annetta</span>: Well, you ought to tell her how much you like her right here, on Love Online. What is her name?\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I don't know her name. I met her online. I just know her online handle.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Host Annetta</span>: Hmmm. Ok. Well, just tell her now. Maybe she's a fan and is listening to the show.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Dr. Dana</span>: Diet soda. You mustn't drink diet soda.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: What? No. Ok. SWEET GIRL. This Friday night, I will be at Bistro 88 at 8:30. I think if you come by we can talk and laugh and really get to know each other. I'll be carrying a large red rose. See you then.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Dr. Annetta</span>: Good luck Peter. Bye.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Bye.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Dr. Dana</span>: Peter remember you must not eat sugar.  I think he'll be ok.", "id": 3}], "audiosrc": "engenn10le10ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le10ob07re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about relationships and personal dilemmas."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what I will have been doing."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express what is necessary."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Who do you go to for advice about dating?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you give good dating advice? Why or why not?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Can you give me some dating advice?"}], "id": 0}, {"type": "STI", "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "